Specifically:

  * The evaluator instructions and the five-level scoring rubrics in
    judge_common.py (HELPFULNESS, CLARITY, COMPLETENESS, GROUNDEDNESS,
    PATH_EFFICIENCY) are copied, with two minor edits noted in the source,
    from libs/amp-evaluation/src/amp_evaluation/evaluators/builtin/llm_judge.py

  * The evidence and execution-step rendering in judge_common.py
    (Trace.format_evidence, Trace.format_steps, ToolCall.__str__) follows
    libs/amp-evaluation/src/amp_evaluation/trace/models.py

  * The output-format block in llm_judge.py (OUTPUT_INSTRUCTIONS) is copied
    from LLMAsJudgeEvaluator._OUTPUT_INSTRUCTIONS in
    libs/amp-evaluation/src/amp_evaluation/evaluators/base.py

  * data/sample_traces.json and data/sample_dataset.json are unmodified
    copies of libs/amp-evaluation/samples/data/

The EvalResult and Trace shapes in judge_common.py are reimplementations of
that library's public contract, written to interoperate with it.

